{"name":"Grullo","hex":"#a99a86","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grullo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colouring of horses characterized by smoky or mouse-colored hairs on the body, often with shoulder and dorsal stripes and black barring on the lower legs.","A horse having this colouring."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grullo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grullo","blocks":[{"text":"Grullo or grulla is a color of horses in the dun family, characterized by tan-gray or mouse-colored hairs on the body, often with shoulder and dorsal stripes and black barring on the lower legs. The genotype for grulla horses is a black base with dun dilution. In this coloration, each individual hair is mouse-colored, unlike a roan, which is composed of a mixture of dark and light hairs. The several shades of grulla are informally referred to with a variety of terms, including black dun, blue dun, slate grulla, silver grulla or light grulla, silver dun, or lobo dun. Silver grulla may also refer to a grulla horse with silver dapple, regardless of shade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/PoneyDun.jpg/330px-PoneyDun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grullo","wikidata":"Q3491937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Steppentarpan.jpg/500px-Steppentarpan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Steppentarpan.jpg/500px-Steppentarpan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Heck horse","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASteppentarpan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Grus_grus_458500626.jpg/500px-Grus_grus_458500626.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Grus_grus_458500626.jpg/1280px-Grus_grus_458500626.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Grus_grus_458500626.jpg/500px-Grus_grus_458500626.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The common crane (Grus grus) is the most common species of crane in Spain and the giver of its name to the grullo color","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrus_grus_458500626.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey bucchero-ware bowl, Clay, 1000-700 BCE, Nr. Babakõy, Turkey, Fitzwilliam Museum, Cambridge","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg/500px-Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl%2C_Clay%2C_1000-700_BCE%2C_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y%2C_Turkey%2C_Fitzwilliam_Museum%2C_Cambridge.jpg","ratio":0.8,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_bucchero-ware_bowl,_Clay,_1000-700_BCE,_Nr._Babak%C3%B5y,_Turkey,_Fitzwilliam_Museum,_Cambridge.jpg","share":0.401875},{"title":"Great Grey Shrike in Bhigwan August 2025 by Tisha Mukherjee 02","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Great_Grey_Shrike_in_Bhigwan_August_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_02.jpg/500px-Great_Grey_Shrike_in_Bhigwan_August_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_02.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Grey_Shrike_in_Bhigwan_August_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_02.jpg","share":0.360625},{"title":"Grey-breasted mountain toucan (Andigena hypoglauca) Caldas","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Grey-breasted_mountain_toucan_%28Andigena_hypoglauca%29_Caldas.jpg/500px-Grey-breasted_mountain_toucan_%28Andigena_hypoglauca%29_Caldas.jpg","ratio":0.7726960896409787,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey-breasted_mountain_toucan